      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T07:01:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s really unclear what this does. It verifies some stuff, but then it triggers an event. It\u0027s not clear why these are grouped in a method ; what do they have to do with each other ? And this is pretty apparent in the naming : I expect you had trouble finding a good name for this method.\n\nFrom the method name maintainers should be able to deduce what the method does. Here, `networkAgentStartedKeepalive` does not suggest it checks anything, nor that it will trigger an event, so it\u0027s not a good name. In fact, it doesn\u0027t really suggest anything ; if I ever saw a method like this I\u0027d think it\u0027s a callback that signals the agent started the keepalive or something.\n\nI think you can\u0027t name this method clearly considering its content. Consider removing the trigger() step from this method, at which point you can call it `verify***` and clarify what it does.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 442,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 442,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "9a797bba90267e18a3de16b11a7a7079da504d78",
