      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-24T06:48:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This name made sense to me as it does 2 things entirely related to the network agent interaction:\n1. It verifies the network agent receives calls to start the socket keepalive.\n2. It simulates whatever callbacks the network agent would trigger as a result of a successful start.\n\nThe name `networkAgentStartedKeepalive` (I think) should imply that this is the expected interaction with the network agent. As opposed to having the `triggerEventKeepalive` separately, it might seem like the trigger event comes out of nowhere.\n\n\u003e if I ever saw a method like this I\u0027d think it\u0027s a callback that signals the agent started the keepalive or something.\n\nThat is the intention, it is what the trigger event does and the additional verify is to ensure the network agent actually gets called to perform the start.\n\nMaybe there is a better name?",
